        <mxCell id="vabRqZXuF9KGcR5PjotK-24" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;" value="Counts: DEV records by type and state (D Demand, BPCR, FR Feature Request); 5 726 in total." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="18" width="520" x="854" y="1168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vabRqZXuF9KGcR5PjotK-25" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;Question:&lt;/b&gt; how does a record move from creation to completion, and who or what moves it?&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; by buttons and request flags that start record-triggered flows; the flows (running as System) write the next state, so the read-only &lt;i&gt;state&lt;/i&gt; field is never edited by hand. One 9-state model is shared by three types.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Findings:&lt;/b&gt; 14 UI actions, 2 request flags, 6 record triggers; Force Execution and Restart are role-gated overrides (role has 0 users on DEV); two demand types (DSC Info only, Digital Accelerator) have no Authorization branch; Feature Request is only a shortcut to Jira; 5 of 12 business rules are empty stubs. No real transition history exists on DEV or TEST (audit data not cloned).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Decisions / to do:&lt;/b&gt; map 9 states and 2 flags to the OOTB demand stages; one mechanism for demand_type paths; keep or retire the overrides; keep or drop Feature Request; read real transition paths on PROD (open)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="105" width="1570" x="-196" y="1202" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
